    {
      "id": "precollege15-d01-morning",
      "title": "Day 1: Morning start",
      "description": "Wake at 07:00. Water, wash up, and spend 10–15 min outdoors in daylight. Keep the phone away during this first block and do not open short-form feeds.\n\nBefore starting study, stand tall but relaxed for 20–30 sec: feet grounded, shoulders easy, chin gently back, no stiff 'military' posture.\n\n📖 Before today's exercise block: if any movement in the exercise task is unfamiliar, check EXERCISE_GUIDE.md (saved with this schedule) or search the YouTube phrase shown in [ ] inside the exercise description.\n\nThe aim is a steadier morning rhythm and clearer attention, not perfect posture.",
      "startTime": "2026-10-08T01:30:00Z",
      "endTime": "2026-10-08T01:50:00Z",
      "durationMinutes": 20,
      "status": "scheduled",
      "priority": "medium",
      "tags": [
        "pre-college",
        "15-day-prep",
        "reworked-v4"
      ],
      "reminders": [],
      "color": "#6366f1",
      "focusMode": false,
      "createdAt": "2026-10-07T19:48:24Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-08T00:20:00Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "precollege15-d01-exercise",
      "title": "Day 1: Exercise",
      "description": "Day 1: Strength A — Baseline\n\nWarm-up (5 min): 2 min easy walk → 6 cat-cow reps [YT: cat cow stretch spine beginners] → 6 slow hip-hinge drills [YT: hip hinge drill tutorial beginners] → 10 shoulder circles each way [YT: shoulder circles warm up exercise].\n\n📖 EXERCISE GUIDE: See EXERCISE_GUIDE.md (saved with this file) or paste any [YT: ...] phrase into YouTube for a video demo.\n\nStrength A — controlled tempo (2 sec down, hold, 2 sec up). Stop 2 reps before failure:\n• 3 × 8–10 bodyweight squats [YT: bodyweight squat form beginners tutorial]\n• 3 × 6–8 push-ups — try the wall or a raised surface first if floor is too hard today [YT: push-up progression beginners elevated]\n• 3 × 10–12 backpack rows — hinge torso ~45°, row pack to lower chest, spine flat [YT: bent over row form beginners tutorial]\n• 3 × 12–15 glute bridges — squeeze glutes firmly at the top, lower slowly [YT: glute bridge exercise tutorial beginners]\n• 3 × 20–25 sec forearm plank — straight body line, breathe normally [YT: plank form beginners forearm]\n• 2 × 5 bird-dogs each side — hold 2 sec at top, keep hips level [YT: bird dog exercise tutorial core stability]\n• 2 × 5 dead bugs each side — lower back pressed to floor throughout [YT: dead bug exercise tutorial lower back]\n\nRest 60–90 sec between sets.\n\n🔴 Stop immediately if: sharp/shooting pain anywhere; chest pressure not easing within ~1 min; dizziness.\n\nBack pain note: Dull muscular tiredness is normal. Sharp or shooting pain = stop that specific exercise for today.\n\nAt 52 kg / 5'10\": Your body is very light — load feels minimal and that is normal. The work is teaching your nervous system to move correctly. Don't skip sets because they feel easy.\n\nCool-down: 3 min easy walk → 3 chin tucks [YT: chin tuck exercise forward head posture] → 5 shoulder rolls.",
      "startTime": "2026-10-08T01:50:00Z",
      "endTime": "2026-10-08T02:30:00Z",
      "durationMinutes": 40,
      "status": "scheduled",
      "priority": "medium",
      "tags": [
        "pre-college",
        "15-day-prep",
        "reworked-v4"
      ],
      "reminders": [],
      "color": "#6366f1",
      "focusMode": false,
      "createdAt": "2026-10-07T19:48:24Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-08T00:20:00Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "precollege15-d01-learning",
      "title": "Day 1: Nursing/science learning",
      "description": "Topic: anatomy vs physiology, homeostasis, anatomical position and directional terms. Use OpenStax A&P 2e Ch. 1: https://openstax.org/books/anatomy-and-physiology-2e/pages/1-introduction Read only the relevant sections; then close it and explain the terms from memory.\nMethod: use the 60-minute learning method from PreCollege_15_Day_Manual.md — learn a small amount, close the source, explain it, then answer questions.\nMovement rule: around the halfway point, stand for 60–90 sec, walk a little, look away from the screen/book, then resume. Do not stay frozen in one sitting posture for the whole hour.",
      "startTime": "2026-10-08T03:30:00Z",
      "endTime": "2026-10-08T04:30:00Z",
      "durationMinutes": 60,
      "status": "scheduled",
      "priority": "medium",
      "tags": [
        "pre-college",
        "15-day-prep",
        "reworked-v4"
      ],
      "reminders": [],
