    {
      "id": "precollege15-d02-exercise",
      "title": "Day 2: Exercise",
      "description": "Day 2: Conditioning\n\n📖 EXERCISE GUIDE: See EXERCISE_GUIDE.md or use any [YT: ...] phrase below.\n\nConditioning: 25 min brisk walking [YT: brisk walking proper form posture] — pace where you can speak short sentences but feel mild breathlessness. Walk on flat ground. Put the phone away — use this time to notice how your posture naturally sits.\n\nPosture/mobility reset after walking (10 min):\n• Cat-cow 8 reps, slow [YT: cat cow stretch spine beginners]\n• Wall slides 2 × 8 — forearms flat to wall throughout [YT: wall slides exercise scapular posture]\n• Bird-dogs 2 × 6 each side — hold 2 sec at top [YT: bird dog exercise tutorial core stability]\n• Chin tucks 2 × 8 — glide chin back, not down [YT: chin tuck exercise forward head posture]\n\n🔴 Stop if: chest tightness or pressure that doesn't ease within 1 min of slowing down; sharp back pain; dizziness.\n\nBack pain note: If your lower back tightens during the walk, slow to easy pace and do 2–3 gentle standing spinal rocks (very slightly forward then upright), then continue.\n\nAt 52 kg / 5'10\": Brisk walking is meaningful cardiovascular conditioning at your current baseline. Don't underestimate it.",
      "startTime": "2026-10-09T01:50:00Z",
      "endTime": "2026-10-09T02:30:00Z",
      "durationMinutes": 40,
      "status": "scheduled",
      "priority": "medium",
      "tags": [
        "pre-college",
        "15-day-prep",
        "reworked-v4"
      ],
      "reminders": [],
      "color": "#6366f1",
      "focusMode": false,
      "createdAt": "2026-10-07T19:48:24Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-08T00:20:00Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "precollege15-d02-learning",
      "title": "Day 2: Nursing/science learning",
      "description": "Topic: levels of organization and major organ systems. Start with OpenStax Ch. 1: https://openstax.org/books/anatomy-and-physiology-2e/pages/1-introduction; use Khan's Human Anatomy & Physiology overview for a visual body-system map: https://www.khanacademy.org/health-and-medicine/human-anatomy-and-physiology. Make a one-page body map, then recall it without looking.\nMethod: use the 60-minute learning method from PreCollege_15_Day_Manual.md — learn a small amount, close the source, explain it, then answer questions.\nMovement rule: around the halfway point, stand for 60–90 sec, walk a little, look away from the screen/book, then resume. Do not stay frozen in one sitting posture for the whole hour.",
      "startTime": "2026-10-09T03:30:00Z",
      "endTime": "2026-10-09T04:30:00Z",
