    {
      "id": "precollege15-d03-exercise",
      "title": "Day 3: Exercise",
      "description": "Day 3: Strength B — Baseline\n\nWarm-up (5 min): Easy walk → cat-cow 6 [YT: cat cow stretch spine beginners] → shoulder circles 10/side [YT: shoulder circles warm up exercise] → 6 hip hinges [YT: hip hinge drill tutorial beginners].\n\n📖 EXERCISE GUIDE: See EXERCISE_GUIDE.md or use [YT: ...] phrases below.\n\nStrength B — controlled tempo throughout:\n• 3 × 6 reverse lunges each leg — use light fingertip wall support for balance [YT: reverse lunge tutorial beginners balance]\n• 3 × 6–8 push-ups — use same surface as Day 1 [YT: push-up progression beginners elevated]\n• 3 × 10–12 backpack rows — hinge forward, back flat, pull to lower chest [YT: bent over row form beginners tutorial]\n• 3 × 15–20 calf raises — slow up (2 sec), hold 1 sec, slow down (3 sec) [YT: calf raise exercise tutorial slow]\n• 3 × 5 dead bugs each side — lower back glued to floor throughout [YT: dead bug exercise tutorial lower back]\n• 2 × 15 sec side plank each side — use knees-on-floor version if needed [YT: side plank beginner modification knees]\n• 2 × 8 hip hinges — push hips back, feel hamstrings, neutral spine [YT: hip hinge strength exercise tutorial]\n\nRest 60–90 sec between sets.\n\n🔴 Stop immediately if: sharp back pain; chest pressure not easing; dizziness.\n\nBack pain note: For rows — keep chest slightly lifted, no rounding at the lower back. For lunges — only go as deep as is pain-free. For hip hinges — feeling it in your hamstrings is correct; feeling it mainly in the lower back means you are rounding slightly.\n\nAt 52 kg / 5'10\": Reverse lunges are a balance challenge before they are a strength challenge at this stage — that is completely normal.\n\nCool-down: 3 min easy walk → open-book thoracic rotations 4/side [YT: open book thoracic rotation exercise] → chin tucks 5.",
      "startTime": "2026-10-10T01:50:00Z",
      "endTime": "2026-10-10T02:30:00Z",
      "durationMinutes": 40,
      "status": "scheduled",
      "priority": "medium",
      "tags": [
        "pre-college",
        "15-day-prep",
        "reworked-v4"
      ],
      "reminders": [],
      "color": "#6366f1",
      "focusMode": false,
      "createdAt": "2026-10-07T19:48:24Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-08T00:20:00Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "precollege15-d03-learning",
      "title": "Day 3: Nursing/science learning",
      "description": "Topic: cell basics — membrane, cytoplasm, nucleus and major organelles. Use OpenStax cell chapter: https://openstax.org/books/anatomy-and-physiology/pages/3-introduction Study a small portion only; draw a simple cell from memory and explain what each selected part does.\nMethod: use the 60-minute learning method from PreCollege_15_Day_Manual.md — learn a small amount, close the source, explain it, then answer questions.\nMovement rule: around the halfway point, stand for 60–90 sec, walk a little, look away from the screen/book, then resume. Do not stay frozen in one sitting posture for the whole hour.",
