    },
    {
      "id": "precollege15-d04-exercise",
      "title": "Day 4: Exercise",
      "description": "Day 4: Conditioning — Intervals\n\n📖 EXERCISE GUIDE: See EXERCISE_GUIDE.md or use [YT: ...] phrases below.\n\nConditioning intervals: 5 min easy walk → 6 rounds of (2 min brisk walk + 1 min easy walk) → 5 min easy walk.\n\nBrisk = you feel the effort but can speak short sentences. Easy = fully comfortable. Start the first 2 rounds at a pace you can maintain for all 6.\n\n🔴 Stop if: chest tightness or pressure not easing within 1 min of slowing; sharp back pain; dizziness.\n\nPosture reset after conditioning (10 min):\n• Cat-cow 6 reps [YT: cat cow stretch spine beginners]\n• Wall slides 2 × 8 [YT: wall slides exercise scapular posture]\n• Bird-dogs 2 × 6 each side [YT: bird dog exercise tutorial core stability]\n• Chin tucks 2 × 8 [YT: chin tuck exercise forward head posture]\n• Hip-flexor stretch 20 sec each side [YT: hip flexor stretch kneeling beginners]\n\nBack pain note: If your lower back tightens during the intervals, reduce brisk sections to 90 sec and extend easy sections to 90 sec.\n\nAt 52 kg / 5'10\": 6 brisk intervals is a step up from Day 2's continuous walk. Pace yourself in the first half.",
      "startTime": "2026-10-11T01:50:00Z",
      "endTime": "2026-10-11T02:30:00Z",
      "durationMinutes": 40,
      "status": "scheduled",
      "priority": "medium",
      "tags": [
        "pre-college",
        "15-day-prep",
        "reworked-v4"
      ],
      "reminders": [],
      "color": "#6366f1",
      "focusMode": false,
      "createdAt": "2026-10-07T19:48:24Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-08T00:20:00Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "precollege15-d04-learning",
      "title": "Day 4: Nursing/science learning",
      "description": "Topic: four main tissue types and structure-function relationships. Use OpenStax tissues chapter: https://openstax.org/books/anatomy-and-physiology-2e/pages/4-introduction Create a small comparison table from memory after learning.\nMethod: use the 60-minute learning method from PreCollege_15_Day_Manual.md — learn a small amount, close the source, explain it, then answer questions.\nMovement rule: around the halfway point, stand for 60–90 sec, walk a little, look away from the screen/book, then resume. Do not stay frozen in one sitting posture for the whole hour.",
      "startTime": "2026-10-11T03:30:00Z",
      "endTime": "2026-10-11T04:30:00Z",
