    {
      "id": "precollege15-d05-exercise",
      "title": "Day 5: Exercise",
      "description": "Day 5: Strength A — Progression\n\nWarm-up (5 min): Easy walk → cat-cow 6 [YT: cat cow stretch spine beginners] → hip hinges 6 [YT: hip hinge drill tutorial beginners] → shoulder circles 10/side [YT: shoulder circles warm up exercise].\n\n📖 EXERCISE GUIDE: See EXERCISE_GUIDE.md or use [YT: ...] phrases below.\n\nStrength A progression — slightly higher reps than Day 1:\n• 3 × 10–12 bodyweight squats [YT: bodyweight squat form beginners tutorial]\n• 3 × 7–9 push-ups — aim for 1 more rep than Day 1 if it feels natural [YT: push-up progression beginners elevated]\n• 3 × 12–15 backpack rows [YT: bent over row form beginners tutorial]\n• 3 × 12–15 glute bridges [YT: glute bridge exercise tutorial beginners]\n• 3 × 25–30 sec forearm plank [YT: plank form beginners forearm]\n• 2 × 6 bird-dogs each side [YT: bird dog exercise tutorial core stability]\n• 2 × 6 dead bugs each side [YT: dead bug exercise tutorial lower back]\n• 2 × 8 controlled hip hinges [YT: hip hinge strength exercise tutorial]\n\nRest 60–90 sec. Leave 2 clean reps in reserve each set — never grind to failure.\n\n🔴 Stop immediately if: sharp/shooting pain; chest pressure not easing; dizziness.\n\nBack pain note: If any rep breaks down in form — reduce range of motion, drop 1–2 reps, rest longer. Form before reps, always.\n\nAt 52 kg / 5'10\": The movements should feel more familiar than Day 1. That improved familiarity is real physical adaptation — motor learning is happening.\n\nCool-down: 3 min easy walk → 5 shoulder rolls → 5 chin tucks [YT: chin tuck exercise forward head posture] → doorway chest stretch 20 sec [YT: doorway chest stretch rounded shoulders posture].",
      "startTime": "2026-10-12T01:50:00Z",
      "endTime": "2026-10-12T02:30:00Z",
      "durationMinutes": 40,
      "status": "scheduled",
      "priority": "medium",
      "tags": [
        "pre-college",
        "15-day-prep",
        "reworked-v4"
      ],
      "reminders": [],
      "color": "#6366f1",
      "focusMode": false,
      "createdAt": "2026-10-07T19:48:24Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-08T00:20:00Z"
    },
