    {
      "id": "precollege15-d06-exercise",
      "title": "Day 6: Exercise",
      "description": "Day 6: Conditioning — Progress\n\n📖 EXERCISE GUIDE: See EXERCISE_GUIDE.md or use [YT: ...] phrases below.\n\nConditioning: 5 min easy walk → 7 rounds of (2 min brisk walk [YT: brisk walking proper form posture] + 1 min easy walk) → 4 min easy walk.\n\nKeep each brisk section at the same pace — don't accelerate. Pace yourself in the first 3 rounds so you can finish the last 4.\n\n🔴 Chest note: Mild breathlessness during brisk walking is normal and expected. Chest tightness or pressure that doesn't ease within ~1 min of slowing = stop for the day and note it.\n\nPosture/mobility reset after walking (10 min):\n• Wall slides 2 × 8 [YT: wall slides exercise scapular posture]\n• Bird-dogs 2 × 7 each side [YT: bird dog exercise tutorial core stability]\n• Chin tucks 2 × 10 [YT: chin tuck exercise forward head posture]\n• Open-book thoracic rotations 2 × 5 each side [YT: open book thoracic rotation exercise]\n\nBack pain note: If back stiffness builds during the walk, reduce brisk sections to 90 sec for the remaining rounds.\n\nAt 52 kg / 5'10\": 7 brisk intervals is a meaningful step up from Day 4's 6 rounds.",
      "startTime": "2026-10-13T01:50:00Z",
      "endTime": "2026-10-13T02:30:00Z",
