    {
      "id": "precollege15-d07-exercise",
      "title": "Day 7: Exercise",
      "description": "Day 7: Active Recovery + Posture — Midpoint\n\n📖 EXERCISE GUIDE: See EXERCISE_GUIDE.md or use [YT: ...] phrases below.\n\nActive recovery — no strength work. Movement and mobility only.\n\n20–25 min easy/comfortable walk — truly easy, not brisk. Every 5 min, do a posture check: head over shoulders, shoulders relaxed and natural (not forced back), breathing normally.\n\nMobility routine after walk (12–15 min):\n• Cat-cow 8 slow reps — 3 sec each position [YT: cat cow stretch spine beginners]\n• Wall slides 2 × 8 [YT: wall slides exercise scapular posture]\n• Open-book thoracic rotations 2 × 5 each side — rotate gently, never force [YT: open book thoracic rotation exercise]\n• Bird-dogs 2 × 6 each side [YT: bird dog exercise tutorial core stability]\n• Chin tucks 2 × 8 [YT: chin tuck exercise forward head posture]\n• Hip-flexor stretch 20 sec each side [YT: hip flexor stretch kneeling beginners]\n• Doorway chest stretch 20 sec [YT: doorway chest stretch rounded shoulders posture]\n\nOptional (2 min): Sit or lie comfortably, breathe in a relaxed natural rhythm. No forced deep breathing. Observe how your chest area feels at rest.\n\nBack pain note: Today should feel relieving, not challenging. If any mobility movement worsens your back, skip it and replace it with extra gentle walking.\n\nAt 52 kg / 5'10\": Recovery days are not wasted days. At your conditioning level, rest and mobility sessions are as important as strength sessions for long-term adaptation.",
      "startTime": "2026-10-14T01:50:00Z",
      "endTime": "2026-10-14T02:30:00Z",
      "durationMinutes": 40,
      "status": "scheduled",
      "priority": "medium",
      "tags": [
