    },
    {
      "id": "precollege15-d08-exercise",
      "title": "Day 8: Exercise",
      "description": "Day 8: Strength B — Progression\n\nWarm-up (5 min): Easy walk → cat-cow 6 [YT: cat cow stretch spine beginners] → hip hinges 6 [YT: hip hinge drill tutorial beginners] → shoulder circles 10/side [YT: shoulder circles warm up exercise].\n\n📖 EXERCISE GUIDE: See EXERCISE_GUIDE.md or use [YT: ...] phrases below.\n\nStrength B progression — higher reps than Day 3:\n• 3 × 7 reverse lunges each leg — use wall support if needed [YT: reverse lunge tutorial beginners balance]\n• 3 × 7–9 push-ups [YT: push-up progression beginners elevated]\n• 3 × 12–14 backpack rows — neutral spine throughout [YT: bent over row form beginners tutorial]\n• 3 × 16–18 calf raises [YT: calf raise exercise tutorial slow]\n• 3 × 7 dead bugs each side — slow and controlled, lower back on floor [YT: dead bug exercise tutorial lower back]\n• 2 × 15–20 sec side plank each side — from knees or feet depending on comfort [YT: side plank beginner modification knees]\n• 2 × 8–10 controlled hip hinges [YT: hip hinge strength exercise tutorial]\n\nRest 60–90 sec between sets.\n\n🔴 Stop immediately if: sharp/shooting pain; chest pressure not easing; dizziness.\n\nBack pain note: For rows — keep chest slightly lifted and spine flat. For lunges — step back only as far as you maintain balance without compensating at the lower back.\n\nAt 52 kg / 5'10\": You're in week 2. Notice if lunges feel more stable than Day 3 — improved balance and coordination is real physical adaptation.\n\nCool-down: 3 min easy walk → open-book rotations 4/side [YT: open book thoracic rotation exercise] → chin tucks 5 → shoulder rolls 5.",
      "startTime": "2026-10-15T01:50:00Z",
      "endTime": "2026-10-15T02:30:00Z",
      "durationMinutes": 40,
      "status": "scheduled",
      "priority": "medium",
      "tags": [
        "pre-college",
        "15-day-prep",
        "reworked-v4"
      ],
      "reminders": [],
