      "description": "Topic: heart structure and blood-flow pathway. Use Khan's circulatory system material: https://www.khanacademy.org/health-and-medicine/human-anatomy-and-physiology. Learn the sequence, then draw the flow from lungs → heart → body → heart → lungs from memory.\nMethod: use the 60-minute learning method from PreCollege_15_Day_Manual.md — learn a small amount, close the source, explain it, then answer questions.\nMovement rule: around the halfway point, stand for 60–90 sec, walk a little, look away from the screen/book, then resume. Do not stay frozen in one sitting posture for the whole hour.",
