    {
      "id": "precollege15-d09-exercise",
      "title": "Day 9: Exercise",
      "description": "Day 9: Conditioning + First Jog Introduction\n\n📖 EXERCISE GUIDE: See EXERCISE_GUIDE.md or use [YT: ...] phrases below.\n\nConditioning with jog introduction: 5 min easy walk → 5 rounds of (3 min brisk walk + 1 min very easy jog + 2 min easy walk) → 3 min easy walk.\n\nThe jog should feel like a barely-faster shuffle — short steps, relaxed shoulders, land mid-foot [YT: slow jogging form beginners tutorial]. If it feels like real effort, you are going too fast. Walking the jog portions is completely acceptable today.\n\n🔴 Chest note: Mild breathlessness is expected and normal. Chest tightness or pressure that doesn't ease within ~1 min = walk the jog portions today and note it.\n\nPosture reset after conditioning:\n• Wall slides 2 × 8 [YT: wall slides exercise scapular posture]\n• Bird-dogs 2 × 6 each side [YT: bird dog exercise tutorial core stability]\n• Chin tucks 2 × 8 [YT: chin tuck exercise forward head posture]\n• Open-book rotations 1 × 5 each side [YT: open book thoracic rotation exercise]\n\nBack pain note: If jogging jars your lower back, walk instead — the cardiovascular goal is heart rate elevation, not the running itself. Walking provides nearly the same benefit at your current level.\n\nAt 52 kg / 5'10\": At your weight, jogging places very low load on your joints. If it still jars your back, focus on your landing — try to land mid-foot rather than heel-strike [YT: proper running form foot strike mid-foot].",
      "startTime": "2026-10-16T01:50:00Z",
      "endTime": "2026-10-16T02:30:00Z",
      "durationMinutes": 40,
      "status": "scheduled",
