    {
      "id": "precollege15-d10-exercise",
      "title": "Day 10: Exercise",
      "description": "Day 10: Strength A — Week 2 Progression\n\nWarm-up (5 min): Easy walk → cat-cow 6 [YT: cat cow stretch spine beginners] → hip hinges 6 [YT: hip hinge drill tutorial beginners] → shoulder circles 10/side [YT: shoulder circles warm up exercise].\n\n📖 EXERCISE GUIDE: See EXERCISE_GUIDE.md or use [YT: ...] phrases below.\n\nStrength A — continuing progression:\n• 3 × 10–12 bodyweight squats — chest up, sit back slightly [YT: bodyweight squat form beginners tutorial]\n• 3 × 8–10 push-ups [YT: push-up progression beginners elevated]\n• 3 × 12–15 backpack rows [YT: bent over row form beginners tutorial]\n• 3 × 12–15 glute bridges [YT: glute bridge exercise tutorial beginners]\n• 3 × 30–35 sec forearm plank [YT: plank form beginners forearm]\n• 2 × 6 bird-dogs each side [YT: bird dog exercise tutorial core stability]\n• 2 × 6 dead bugs each side [YT: dead bug exercise tutorial lower back]\n• 2 × 10 controlled hip hinges [YT: hip hinge strength exercise tutorial]\n\nRest 60–90 sec. Quality over speed — never rush through a set.\n\n🔴 Stop immediately if: sharp/shooting pain; chest pressure not easing; dizziness.\n\nBack pain note: Compare how your back feels during hip hinges and planks now vs. Day 1. Any reduction in stiffness during these movements is a sign of real adaptation. If the plank still bothers your lower back, use the knees-on-floor version [YT: plank on knees modification beginners].\n\nAt 52 kg / 5'10\": Aim for 1 more clean rep per set vs. Day 5, only if it feels natural. Don't force it — movement quality matters more than rep counts.\n\nCool-down: 3 min easy walk → hip-flexor stretch 20 sec/side [YT: hip flexor stretch kneeling beginners] → doorway chest stretch 20 sec [YT: doorway chest stretch rounded shoulders posture].",
      "startTime": "2026-10-17T01:50:00Z",
      "endTime": "2026-10-17T02:30:00Z",
      "durationMinutes": 40,
      "status": "scheduled",
      "priority": "medium",
