      "updatedAt": "2026-10-08T00:20:00Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "precollege15-d11-exercise",
      "title": "Day 11: Exercise",
      "description": "Day 11: Conditioning — Higher Volume\n\n📖 EXERCISE GUIDE: See EXERCISE_GUIDE.md or use [YT: ...] phrases below.\n\nConditioning: 5 min easy walk → 8 rounds of (2 min brisk walk [YT: brisk walking proper form posture] + 1 min easy walk) → 5 min easy walk.\n\nThis is the highest round count of the entire program. Start the first 3 rounds at a pace you can hold for all 8 — don't go fast early.\n\n🔴 Chest note: Mild breathlessness during brisk walking is expected. Tightness or pressure that doesn't ease when you slow down = walk easy and monitor; stop if it doesn't settle.\n\nPosture reset after conditioning:\n• Wall slides 2 × 10 [YT: wall slides exercise scapular posture]\n• Bird-dogs 2 × 7 each side [YT: bird dog exercise tutorial core stability]\n• Chin tucks 2 × 10 [YT: chin tuck exercise forward head posture]\n• Open-book rotations 1 × 5 each side [YT: open book thoracic rotation exercise]\n• Hip-flexor stretch 20 sec each side [YT: hip flexor stretch kneeling beginners]\n\nBack pain note: 8 rounds is a cumulative load on your back. If it stiffens toward the last 2 rounds, reduce those to easy walking only.\n\nAt 52 kg / 5'10\": 8 rounds is a significant step up from Day 6's 7 rounds. Pace matters more than speed.",
      "startTime": "2026-10-18T01:50:00Z",
      "endTime": "2026-10-18T02:30:00Z",
      "durationMinutes": 40,
      "status": "scheduled",
      "priority": "medium",
      "tags": [
        "pre-college",
