    },
    {
      "id": "precollege15-d11-learning",
      "title": "Day 11: Nursing/science learning",
      "description": "Topic: nervous system — neuron and major divisions. Use Khan's nervous-system introduction: https://www.khanacademy.org/health-and-medicine/human-anatomy-and-physiology. Build a simple hierarchy and explain what the system is broadly responsible for.\nMethod: use the 60-minute learning method from PreCollege_15_Day_Manual.md — learn a small amount, close the source, explain it, then answer questions.\nMovement rule: around the halfway point, stand for 60–90 sec, walk a little, look away from the screen/book, then resume. Do not stay frozen in one sitting posture for the whole hour.",
