    {
      "id": "precollege15-d12-exercise",
      "title": "Day 12: Exercise",
      "description": "Day 12: Strength B — Final Progression\n\nWarm-up (5 min): Easy walk → cat-cow 6 [YT: cat cow stretch spine beginners] → hip hinges 6 [YT: hip hinge drill tutorial beginners] → shoulder circles 10/side [YT: shoulder circles warm up exercise].\n\n📖 EXERCISE GUIDE: See EXERCISE_GUIDE.md or use [YT: ...] phrases below.\n\nStrength B — the most advanced version of this session:\n• 3 × 8 reverse lunges each leg [YT: reverse lunge tutorial beginners balance]\n• 3 × 8–10 push-ups [YT: push-up progression beginners elevated]\n• 3 × 13–15 backpack rows [YT: bent over row form beginners tutorial]\n• 3 × 18–20 calf raises [YT: calf raise exercise tutorial slow]\n• 3 × 8 dead bugs each side [YT: dead bug exercise tutorial lower back]\n• 2 × 20 sec side plank each side — from feet or knees [YT: side plank beginner modification knees]\n• 2 × 10 controlled hip hinges [YT: hip hinge strength exercise tutorial]\n\nRest 60–90 sec. Still leaving 1–2 reps in reserve — not going to failure.\n\n🔴 Stop immediately if: sharp/shooting pain; chest pressure not easing; dizziness.\n\nBack pain note: Compare how your back feels during hip hinges and rows now vs. Day 3 and Day 8. Any reduction in stiffness or discomfort during these specific movements is meaningful physical progress.\n\nAt 52 kg / 5'10\": If lunges and push-ups feel more natural and less exhausting than Day 3, that is real strength and coordination improvement — not imagined.\n\nCool-down: 3 min easy walk → open-book rotations 4/side [YT: open book thoracic rotation exercise] → chin tucks 5 → shoulder rolls 5.",
      "startTime": "2026-10-19T01:50:00Z",
      "endTime": "2026-10-19T02:30:00Z",
      "durationMinutes": 40,
      "status": "scheduled",
