      "id": "precollege15-d13-exercise",
      "title": "Day 13: Exercise",
      "description": "Day 13: Conditioning + Extended Jog\n\n📖 EXERCISE GUIDE: See EXERCISE_GUIDE.md or use [YT: ...] phrases below.\n\nConditioning with extended jog: 5 min easy walk → 4 rounds of (3 min brisk walk + 2 min very easy jog [YT: slow jogging form beginners tutorial] + 2 min easy walk) → 4 min easy walk.\n\nJog sections are 2 min today (vs. 1 min on Day 9). If 2 min feels too long, do 90 sec jog + 30 sec walk — that is completely fine. Walking the jog sections is always the acceptable fallback, not a failure.\n\n🔴 Chest note: Same monitoring as Day 9. Mild breathlessness is expected. Tightness or pressure not easing within ~1 min = walk the jog sections today and note it.\n\nPosture reset after conditioning:\n• Wall slides 2 × 10 [YT: wall slides exercise scapular posture]\n• Bird-dogs 2 × 7 each side [YT: bird dog exercise tutorial core stability]\n• Chin tucks 2 × 10 [YT: chin tuck exercise forward head posture]\n• Open-book rotations 1 × 5 each side [YT: open book thoracic rotation exercise]\n\nBack pain note: If jogging causes lower-back jarring today, walk those sections and focus on brisk walking form instead. The cardiovascular benefit is nearly the same at your level.\n\nAt 52 kg / 5'10\": You started this program not jogging at all. Reaching 2-min jog sections — even at a slow shuffle — is genuine cardiovascular progress regardless of pace.",
      "startTime": "2026-10-20T01:50:00Z",
      "endTime": "2026-10-20T02:30:00Z",
      "durationMinutes": 40,
      "status": "scheduled",
      "priority": "medium",
