      "createdAt": "2026-10-07T19:48:24Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-08T00:20:00Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "precollege15-d14-exercise",
      "title": "Day 14: Exercise",
      "description": "Day 14: Active Recovery + Final Mobility\n\n📖 EXERCISE GUIDE: See EXERCISE_GUIDE.md or use [YT: ...] phrases below.\n\nActive recovery — same structure as Day 7, slightly more thorough.\n\n25–30 min easy/comfortable walk — not brisk, truly easy. Use it to practice everything you've learned: relaxed upright head, shoulders easy and natural (not forced back), normal breathing rhythm.\n\nMobility routine after walk (10–12 min):\n• Cat-cow 8 slow reps [YT: cat cow stretch spine beginners]\n• Wall slides 2 × 10 [YT: wall slides exercise scapular posture]\n• Open-book thoracic rotations 2 × 5 each side [YT: open book thoracic rotation exercise]\n• Bird-dogs 2 × 7 each side [YT: bird dog exercise tutorial core stability]\n• Chin tucks 2 × 10 [YT: chin tuck exercise forward head posture]\n• Doorway chest stretch 20 sec [YT: doorway chest stretch rounded shoulders posture]\n• Hip-flexor stretch 20 sec each side [YT: hip flexor stretch kneeling beginners]\n\nOptional (2 min): Sit or lie comfortably. Breathe in a natural, relaxed rhythm — no forcing. Observe how your chest area feels at rest compared to Day 7.\n\nBack pain note: Notice your baseline back stiffness today compared to Day 7. Any reduction in resting stiffness after 2 weeks of consistent movement is real progress.\n\nAt 52 kg / 5'10\": Rest well tonight. Tomorrow's session is intentionally not a maximum-effort test — it is a comparison, not a competition.",
      "startTime": "2026-10-21T01:50:00Z",
      "endTime": "2026-10-21T02:30:00Z",
      "durationMinutes": 40,
      "status": "scheduled",
      "priority": "medium",
      "tags": [
        "pre-college",
