    },
    {
      "id": "precollege15-d14-learning",
      "title": "Day 14: Nursing/science learning",
      "description": "Topic: infection-prevention foundations. Read WHO 'Hand Hygiene: Why, How & When?' (https://www.who.int/publications/m/item/hand-hygiene-why-how-when) and CDC Standard Precautions (https://www.cdc.gov/infection-control/hcp/basics/standard-precautions.html). Learn the reasons and key situations; do not self-teach clinical procedure technique.\nMethod: use the 60-minute learning method from PreCollege_15_Day_Manual.md — learn a small amount, close the source, explain it, then answer questions.\nMovement rule: around the halfway point, stand for 60–90 sec, walk a little, look away from the screen/book, then resume. Do not stay frozen in one sitting posture for the whole hour.",
      "startTime": "2026-10-21T03:30:00Z",
