    },
    {
      "id": "precollege15-d15-exercise",
      "title": "Day 15: Exercise",
      "description": "Day 15: Final Comparison Session — Not a Test\n\nWarm-up (5 min): Easy walk → cat-cow 6 [YT: cat cow stretch spine beginners] → hip hinges 6 [YT: hip hinge drill tutorial beginners] → shoulder circles 10/side [YT: shoulder circles warm up exercise].\n\n📖 EXERCISE GUIDE: See EXERCISE_GUIDE.md or use [YT: ...] phrases below.\n\nFinal comparison — do this the same way you did Day 1 and notice how it feels. Do not try to maximise reps.\n\n3 controlled rounds of:\n• 10 bodyweight squats [YT: bodyweight squat form beginners tutorial]\n• 6–8 push-ups — use the same surface as Day 1 if possible [YT: push-up progression beginners elevated]\n• 12 backpack rows [YT: bent over row form beginners tutorial]\n• 12 glute bridges [YT: glute bridge exercise tutorial beginners]\n• 25–30 sec forearm plank [YT: plank form beginners forearm]\nRest ~90 sec between rounds.\n\nThen:\n• 2 × 8 hip hinges [YT: hip hinge strength exercise tutorial]\n• 2 × 7 bird-dogs each side [YT: bird dog exercise tutorial core stability]\n• 2 × 8 dead bugs each side [YT: dead bug exercise tutorial lower back]\n• 2 × 8 chin tucks [YT: chin tuck exercise forward head posture]\n• 2 × 8 wall slides [YT: wall slides exercise scapular posture]\n\nNotice (don't judge): Does your back feel more or less stiff during squats and hinges than on Day 1? Do you need to concentrate as hard on push-up form? Do the bird-dogs feel more controlled?\n\n🔴 Still stop immediately if: sharp/shooting pain; chest pressure not easing; dizziness.\n\nBack pain note: If your back has felt better overall over these 15 days — less morning stiffness, less discomfort during movements — that is the most important physical outcome of this program.\n\nAt 52 kg / 5'10\": 15 days of consistent daily movement is a real foundation. You have built movement familiarity, basic conditioning, and trunk tolerance. That matters and it carries forward into college.\n\nCool-down: 5 min easy walk → open-book rotations 4/side [YT: open book thoracic rotation exercise] → chin tucks 5 → shoulder rolls 5.",
      "startTime": "2026-10-22T01:50:00Z",
      "endTime": "2026-10-22T02:30:00Z",
      "durationMinutes": 40,
      "status": "scheduled",
      "priority": "medium",
