    {
      "id": "precollege15-d15-learning",
      "title": "Day 15: Nursing/science learning",
      "description": "Cumulative final retrieval. Without looking, explain the body map, homeostasis, cells, tissues, bones, circulation, respiration, nervous/endocrine systems and basic nursing-safety concepts. Then check your gaps using the sources listed in this program.\nMethod: use the 60-minute learning method from PreCollege_15_Day_Manual.md — learn a small amount, close the source, explain it, then answer questions.\nMovement rule: around the halfway point, stand for 60–90 sec, walk a little, look away from the screen/book, then resume. Do not stay frozen in one sitting posture for the whole hour.",
