    {
      "id": "precollege15-d15-retention",
      "title": "Day 15: Retrieval and retention",
      "description": "Final retention check: closed-book recall first, then answer 10–15 mixed questions. Compare with the first-week baseline: how many concepts can you explain without cues, where do you still rely on recognition, and which topics fail under retrieval? Review only failures. Finish by writing 3 rules for continuing this system in college: active recall, spaced reviews, and question practice.",
